      "problem": "If $X=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $Y=\\{a\\}$ then $|P(X\\times Y)|=$",
      "worked_solution": "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|X|=3,\\,|Y|=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(X\\times Y)| & ={2}^{|X\\times Y|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|X|\\,\\cdot \\,|Y|} \\\\  & ={2}^{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & ={2}^{3} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
